#. Tag: title
#: dcop.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scripting &kmplot;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dcop.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A new feature in &kde; 3.4 is that you can write scrips for &kmplot; with "
"&DCOP;. For example, if you want to define a new function <userinput>f(x)"
"=2sin x+3cos x</userinput>, set its line width to 20 and then draw it, you "
"type in a console:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dcop.docbook:5
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>dcop kmplot-PID Parser addFunction \"f(x)=2sin x+3cos x\"</command> "
"As a result, the new function's id number will be returned, or -1 if the "
"function could not be defined."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dcop.docbook:7
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>>dcop kmplot-PID Parser setFunctionFLineWidth 20 ID</command> This "
"command sets the function with the id number ID the line width to 20."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dcop.docbook:9
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>>dcop kmplot-PID View drawPlot</command> This command repaints the "
"window so that the function get visible."
msgstr ""

